# Data drive (`/data`) — keep root SSD free

Automation host `192.168.2.4`:

| Disk | Mount | Role |
|------|-------|------|
| `/dev/sda` (~15 GB) | `/` | OS + `/opt` only |
| `/dev/sdb` (~120 GB) | `/data` | Logs, swap, snapshots, backups |

## Required behavior

1. **Never** leave unbounded logs on `/` (Home Assistant previously filled the root disk with `home-assistant.log`).
2. After disk work or deploy, ensure `/data` is mounted and run:
   `sudo bash /opt/dell_server_management/scripts/server/setup_data_drive_logs.sh`
3. Keep `cleanup-root-disk.timer` enabled (target ≤ 80% on `/`).
4. New large artifacts (logs, DBs, snapshots, images) go under `/data/…`, not `/var` or `/home` on root.
5. Home Assistant config lives on `/data/homeassistant/config` (bind-mounted); do not write large HA state back onto the root SSD.

Docs: [docs/developer/SERVER_DISK.md](docs/developer/SERVER_DISK.md).
